 inputs a function of the log at the contribution's own seq, so computing and storing them during Apply is the only way replay reproduces every schedule row byte for byte; the planned ScheduleAuditJob was therefore unnecessary, and outcome_is_unusual is judged under the default model as of that seq so a later model release cannot change past decisions."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_07_audits_challenged_contributions_do_not_count", "label": "Challenged contributions do not count until confirmed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-07-audits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Audits::Status derives, as of any seq, whether a compromise window or a latest-UNRESOLVED audit covers a contribution with no later CONFIRMED audit, and Scoring::BuildInput drops such links, so doubt suppresses evidence rather than silently discounting it."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_07_audits_restoration_creates_new_rows", "label": "Re-audit restores by creating new rows", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-07-audits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A disagreeing RE_AUDIT invalidates the first audit and its reputation event and the system appends an ACCEPT with basis RESTORED_AFTER_RE_AUDIT; Ledger::Restore recreates the invalidated rows as new rows with ids derived from the restoring ACCEPT and created_seq at that seq, so history shows the gap instead of hiding it."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_07_audits_reputation_is_not_a_scoring_input", "label": "Reputation is audit-derived and not a scoring input", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-07-audits.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationa